  TR["VN-H074"] = {
    "lawId": "VN-H074",
    "sourceLang": "zh",
    "targetLang": "en",
    "engine": "llm",
    "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash",
    "promptVersion": "calr-vi2en-v1",
    "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
    "reviewed": "machine",
    "completenessNote": "逐条对译，共 51 条；条号与原文一一对应，未合并、未省略。",
    "articles": [
      {
        "no": 1,
        "text": {
          "en": "Belt and Road Legal Research, Volume 3 ·204· The Law on Counter-Terrorism of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam Pursuant to the 1992 Constitution of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, as amended and supplemented by Resolution No. 51/2001/QH10, the National Assembly hereby promulgates the Law on Counter-Terrorism.\nChapter I GENERAL PROVISIONS\n[Scope of regulation] This Law provides for the principles, policies, measures and forces of counter-terrorism, international cooperation in counter-terrorism and the responsibilities of agencies, organisations and individuals."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 1"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 2,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Subjects of application] This Law applies to Vietnamese citizens, agencies and organisations; and to international organisations, foreign organisations and foreigners residing and carrying out activities in Vietnam, except where otherwise provided for by international treaties to which the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is a party."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 2"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 3,
        "text": {
          "en": "Interpretation of terms In this Law, the following terms shall be construed as follows:\n1. Terrorism means acts of organisations or individuals aimed at opposing the people's administration, forcing the people's administration, foreign organisations or international organisations, obstructing the international relations of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam or causing public panic, including:\n(1) infringing upon the life, health or personal liberty of another person or threatening to infringe upon the life or mental well-being of another person;\n(2) appropriating, damaging, destroying or threatening to destroy the property of agencies, organisations or individuals; attacking, infringing upon, obstructing or disrupting the operation of the computer networks, telecommunications networks, the Internet and digital equipment of agencies, organisations or individuals;\n(3) guiding the manufacture, production or use of, or manufacturing, producing, stockpiling, transporting or trading in, weapons, explosives, radioactive substances, toxic substances, inflammable substances and other articles and means used to commit the acts provided for in points (1) and (2) of clause 1 of this Article;\n(4) propagating, inducing, inciting, coercing or hiring another person to commit, or facilitating or assisting the commission of, the acts provided for in points (1) and (2) of clause 1 of this Article;\n(5) establishing or joining an organisation, recruiting, training or drilling persons to commit the acts provided for in points (1), (2), (3) and (4) of clause 1 of this Article;\n* Translator: Tao Wenwen, doctoral student at the School of Asian Studies, Beijing Foreign Studies University.\n* ·205· The Law on Counter-Terrorism of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam\n(6) other terrorist acts provided for by international treaties on counter-terrorism to which the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is a party.\n2. Terrorist financing means the raising and provision of funds and property, in any form, for terrorist organisations and individuals.\n3. Counter-terrorism comprises activities to prevent terrorism and terrorist financing and activities to combat terrorism and terrorist financing."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 3"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 4,
        "text": {
          "en": "Principles of counter-terrorism\n1. The people's public security forces shall act as the core, in coordination with the people's army, under the leadership of the Communist Party of Vietnam, the unified management of the State and the participation of the whole society.\n2. Compliance with the Constitution and the law and assurance of the independence, sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity of the Fatherland, of national interests and of the lawful rights and interests of agencies, organisations and individuals.\n3. Prevention shall be the principal approach, with proactive detection, timely prevention and strict handling of organisations and individuals engaged in terrorism and terrorist financing.\n4. Protection of the safety of the life and health of the people and of the property of agencies and organisations, and minimisation of losses."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 4"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 5,
        "text": {
          "en": "Policy on counter-terrorism\n1. The State shall try and severely punish all acts of terrorism and terrorist financing and shall take synchronous measures to organise counter-terrorism work and to disseminate information on and mobilise organisations and individuals to participate in counter-terrorism activities.\n2. The State shall adopt policies to mobilise scientific and technological achievements in the service of counter-terrorism activities.\n3. The State shall give priority to investment in specialised technical equipment and means for the counter-terrorism and counter-terrorist financing forces and shall provide institutional and policy guarantees for such forces.\n4. The State shall adopt policies and measures to protect organisations and individuals participating in counter-terrorism activities. Where a person participating in counter-terrorism activities suffers physical injury or harm to health or dies, he or she or his or her relatives shall be entitled to the preferential regimes and policies provided for by law. Where the property of an organisation or individual that has been mobilised in the service of counter-terrorism activities is damaged, compensation shall be paid.\n5. Organisations and individuals with meritorious achievements in counter-terrorism activities shall be commended in accordance with the law on emulation and commendation.\n6. The State shall adopt a lenient policy towards organisations and individuals that voluntarily abandon the intention to commit terrorism or terrorist financing; that voluntarily desist from the commission of acts of terrorism or terrorist financing; or that, before acts of terrorism or terrorist financing are reported, actively prevent or mitigate the harm, remedy the consequences and surrender themselves and report truthfully and actively assist the responsible agencies in detecting, stopping, investigating, prosecuting and trying terrorism and terrorist financing."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 5"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 6,
        "text": {
          "en": "Prohibited acts\n1. Acts of terrorism and terrorist financing provided for in clauses 1 and 2 of Article 3 of this Law.\n2. Concealing, harbouring or failing to denounce terrorism or terrorist financing.\nBelt and Road Legal Research, Volume 3 ·206·\n3. Disclosing State secrets in counter-terrorism work.\n4. Deliberately spreading false information on terrorism or terrorist financing, obstructing or hindering counter-terrorism activities.\n5. Abusing the functions and powers of counter-terrorism work to infringe upon national interests and the lawful rights and interests of organisations and individuals."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 6"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 7,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibility for counter-terrorism\n1. Counter-terrorism is the responsibility of agencies, organisations and citizens.\n2. Heads of agencies and persons in charge of organisations shall, within the scope of their functions and powers, be responsible for implementing the law on counter-terrorism.\n3. International organisations, foreign organisations and foreigners residing and carrying out activities in Vietnam shall be responsible for participating in counter-terrorism activities in accordance with this Law and other relevant laws."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 7"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 8,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Responsibilities of the Vietnam Fatherland Front and its member organisations] The Vietnam Fatherland Front and its member organisations shall, within the scope of their functions and powers, be responsible for disseminating information on and mobilising the people to strictly implement the law on counter-terrorism and for supervising the implementation of the law on counter-terrorism."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 8"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 9,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Investigation, prosecution and trial of terrorist offenders and terrorist financing offenders] The investigation, prosecution and trial of terrorist offenders and terrorist financing offenders shall comply with the provisions of the Penal Code, the Criminal Procedure Code and other relevant laws."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 9"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 10,
        "text": {
          "en": "Handling of funds and property related to terrorism and terrorist financing\n1. Funds and property related to terrorism and terrorist financing shall be subject to suspension of circulation, blocking, sealing, temporary seizure and handling in accordance with law.\n2. The Government shall make specific provisions on the conditions, procedures, competence and forms of suspension of circulation, blocking, sealing, temporary seizure and handling of funds and property related to terrorism and terrorist financing."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 10"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 11,
        "text": {
          "en": "Funding for ensuring counter-terrorism activities\n1. The sources of funding for ensuring counter-terrorism activities comprise:\n(1) the State budget;\n(2) other lawful sources of funding.\n2. The management and use of funding for ensuring counter-terrorism activities shall comply with the provisions of law.\nChapter II ORGANISATION OF COUNTER-TERRORISM ACTIVITIES"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 11"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 12,
        "text": {
          "en": "Steering committees for counter-terrorism\n1. The Government shall establish the National Steering Committee for Counter-Terrorism, whose members shall work on a part-time basis.\n2. The Ministry of Public Security shall be the standing body of the National Steering Committee for Counter-Terrorism and shall have a full-time advisory and assisting body.\n3. Provincial People's Committees shall establish provincial steering committees for counter-terrorism. The ·207· The Law on Counter-Terrorism of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam members of provincial steering committees for counter-terrorism shall work on a part-time basis.\nThe provincial Public Security Department shall be the standing body of the provincial steering committee for counter-terrorism and shall have an advisory and assisting body.\n4. On the basis of the tasks assigned and the direction given by the Prime Minister, ministers and heads of ministerial-level agencies shall establish ministerial steering committees for counter-terrorism."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 12"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 13,
        "text": {
          "en": "Tasks and powers of the steering committees for counter-terrorism\n1. The tasks and powers of the National Steering Committee for Counter-Terrorism are as follows:\n(1) to advise the Government and the Prime Minister on the organisation and direction of counter-terrorism activities throughout the country;\n(2) to assist the Government and the Prime Minister in organising the implementation of intersectoral coordination and international cooperation in counter-terrorism;\n(3) to assist the Government and the Prime Minister in inspecting, urging and directing counter-terrorism work.\n2. The tasks and powers of the provincial steering committees for counter-terrorism are as follows:\n(1) to advise the People's Committee and the Chairman of the People's Committee at the same level on the organisation and direction of local counter-terrorism activities;\n(2) to assist the People's Committee and the Chairman of the People's Committee at the same level in organising the implementation of local intersectoral coordination in counter-terrorism;\n(3) to assist the People's Committee and the Chairman of the People's Committee at the same level in inspecting, urging and directing counter-terrorism work.\n3. The ministerial steering committees for counter-terrorism shall assist ministers and heads of ministerial-level agencies in organising and directing counter-terrorism work in the fields under their charge and shall coordinate with other ministries, localities and agencies in carrying out counter-terrorism work.\n4. The Government shall make specific provisions on the organisation, tasks, powers and coordinating relationships of the steering committees for counter-terrorism at all levels."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 13"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 14,
        "text": {
          "en": "Counter-terrorism forces\n1. The counter-terrorism forces comprise:\n(1) the agencies and units under the Ministry of Public Security and the Ministry of National Defence that are assigned the task of carrying out counter-terrorism;\n(2) other forces mobilised to participate in counter-terrorism.\n2. The Minister of Public Security and the Minister of National Defence shall make specific provisions on the tasks and powers of the agencies and units provided for in point (1) of clause 1 of this Article."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 14"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 15,
        "text": {
          "en": "Counter-terrorism commanders\n1. Counter-terrorism commanders shall be decided by the competent agency.\n2. Where the competent agency has not yet decided on a counter-terrorism commander, the persons in charge of the State agencies, people's armed forces and People's Committees at the place where the terrorist activity occurs shall be responsible for taking counter-terrorism measures in accordance with"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 15"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 16,
        "text": {
          "en": "clause 2 of this Article.\n3. Where a terrorist activity occurs on an aircraft or a vessel after it has left an airport or a port, the person in command of the means of transport shall be responsible for directing counter-terrorism work.\n4. The Government shall make detailed provisions on the content of this Article.\nBelt and Road Legal Research, Volume 3 ·208·\nArticle 16 Tasks and powers of counter-terrorism commanders\n1. The counter-terrorism commanders provided for in clause 1 of Article 15 of this Law shall have the following tasks and powers:\n(1) to provide staff advice and proposals to the competent agency in deciding on necessary counter-terrorism plans and measures;\n(2) to direct counter-terrorism work in accordance with the plans and measures decided by the competent agency;\n(3) where an urgent situation arises but the competent agency has not yet decided on plans and measures, to be responsible for taking the measures provided for in clause 2 of Article 30 of this Law, except where such measures have political and diplomatic implications, infringe upon the life of another person or destroy property of special value.\n2. The persons in charge of the State agencies, people's armed forces and People's Committees provided for in clause 2 of Article 15 of this Law shall be responsible for taking the urgent counter-terrorism measures provided for in points (1), (2), (3), (4), (6), (7), (8) and (11) of clause 2 of Article 30 of this Law, except where such measures have political and diplomatic implications, infringe upon the life of another person or destroy property of special value.\n3. The persons in command of counter-terrorism provided for in clause 3 of Article 15 of this Law shall be responsible for taking measures to prevent and stop terrorist acts in accordance with law.\n4. The persons provided for in clauses 1, 2 and 3 of this Article shall bear legal responsibility for their acts and decisions."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 16"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 17,
        "text": {
          "en": "Equipping and use of weapons, supporting tools and means for counter-terrorism\n1. The counter-terrorism forces shall be given priority in being equipped with weapons, supporting tools and specialised technical means for counter-terrorism.\n2. The use of weapons, supporting tools and specialised technical means by the counter-terrorism forces shall comply with the provisions of this Law and other relevant laws."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 17"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 18,
        "text": {
          "en": "Mobilisation of forces and means for counter-terrorism, and requisition and acquisition of property for counter-terrorism\n1. Where a terrorist activity occurs, persons with competence provided for by law may mobilise forces and means to combat terrorism.\nAgencies, organisations and individuals mobilised to carry out counter-terrorism activities shall be responsible for complying.\n2. Where a terrorist activity occurs, the requisition and acquisition of property for counter-terrorism shall comply with the provisions of the law on requisition and acquisition of property.\nChapter III PREVENTION OF TERRORISM"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 18"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 19,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Measures for the prevention of terrorism] The measures for preventing terrorism and terrorist financing shall be those provided for in Articles 19"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 19"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 20,
        "text": {
          "en": "to 27 of this Law and other measures provided for by law.\nArticle 20 Notification, dissemination and education on counter-terrorism\n1. Competent agencies and persons shall be responsible for carrying out notification, dissemination and education on counter-terrorism so as to raise awareness of, the sense of responsibility for and the effectiveness of counter-terrorism.\n·209· The Law on Counter-Terrorism of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam\n2. The content of notification, dissemination and education on counter-terrorism comprises:\n(1) the risks, developments and situation of terrorism, and the means, methods, danger and harm of terrorist activities;\n(2) measures, experience, policies and laws on counter-terrorism;\n(3) the responsibilities of agencies, organisations and individuals in counter-terrorism activities;\n(4) other necessary content on counter-terrorism."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 20"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 21,
        "text": {
          "en": "Administrative management of public order\n1. Competent agencies and persons conducting administrative management of public order through their activities shall be responsible for proactively and promptly detecting the causes, conditions, plots, methods, means and activities of terrorist organisations and individuals and for taking corresponding handling measures.\n2. Measures for the prevention of terrorism through administrative management of public order comprise:\n(1) management of the residence, records and identity information of citizens;\n(2) management of weapons, explosives, supporting tools, inflammable substances, toxic substances and radioactive substances;\n(3) guarding and protecting important works in Vietnam relating to national security, national defence works, military zones, the offices of diplomatic missions, foreign consular institutions and the representative offices of international organisations;\n(4) patrolling, supervising and monitoring key targets relating to public order, airports, ports, railway stations, bus stations, border gates, border areas, places where people gather and other public places;\n(5) management of entry, exit and transit;\n(6) other measures of administrative management of public order provided for by law."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 21"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 22,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Supervision of transport activities] Competent agencies and persons supervising road, railway, inland waterway, maritime and air transport shall be responsible for proactively detecting, promptly stopping and handling the use of such modes of transport for terrorist activities."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 22"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 23,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Supervision of transactions in funds and property] Competent agencies and persons supervising transactions in funds and property shall be responsible for paying attention to, monitoring and stopping transactions in funds and property that show signs of terrorism, and for supervising transactions in funds and property of a value subject to reporting in accordance with law so as to promptly detect transactions showing signs of terrorism."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 23"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 24,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Supervision of means and goods entering, leaving or transiting the country] Competent agencies and persons supervising means and goods entering, leaving or transiting the country shall be responsible for strictly supervising means and goods entering, leaving or transiting the country so as to promptly detect, stop and handle the use of such means for terrorist activities."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 24"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 25,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Supervision of publication, the press, postal services, telecommunications and other forms of information] Competent agencies and persons engaged in activities relating to publication, the press, postal services, telecommunications and other forms of information shall be responsible for supervising, and promptly detecting, stopping and handling, the use of such activities for terrorist activities.\nBelt and Road Legal Research, Volume 3 ·210·"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 25"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 26,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Supervision of activities to ensure the hygiene and safety of food and of medicines for disease prevention and treatment] Competent agencies and persons supervising the hygiene and safety of foodstuffs, food, animal feed, fertilisers, medicines for treatment, medicines for prevention, veterinary medicines, plant protection medicines and laboratory specimens shall be responsible for promptly detecting, stopping and handling the use of such items for terrorist activities."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 26"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 27,
        "text": {
          "en": "Formulation and organisation of the implementation of plans for counter-terrorism\n1. The Ministry of Public Security, the Ministry of National Defence, the relevant ministries and People's Committees at all levels shall, within the scope of their responsibilities, be responsible for formulating, drilling, exercising and organising the implementation of plans for counter-terrorism.\n2. The agencies, organisations and units identified in an approved plan for counter-terrorism shall be responsible for complying.\nChapter IV COMBATING TERRORISM"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 27"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 28,
        "text": {
          "en": "Detection of terrorism\n1. Agencies, organisations and individuals shall proactively detect terrorism through their activities.\n2. The counter-terrorism forces provided for in point (1) of clause 1 of Article 14 of this Law shall be responsible for taking specialised technical measures to detect terrorism and for guiding and assisting agencies, organisations and individuals in identifying, detecting, notifying and denouncing terrorist activities."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 28"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 29,
        "text": {
          "en": "Receipt and handling of notifications and denunciations of terrorism\n1. Where agencies, organisations or individuals detect signs or acts of terrorism, they shall promptly notify the counter-terrorism forces provided for in point\n(1) of clause 1 of Article 14 of this Law or the nearest public security office, military unit or People's Committee. Public security offices, military units and People's Committees shall be responsible for receiving in full notifications and denunciations concerning terrorism.\n2. Upon receiving a notification or denunciation concerning terrorism as provided for in clause 1 of this Article, or upon detecting signs and acts of terrorism on their own, public security offices, military units and People's Committees shall immediately notify the counter-terrorism forces provided for in point (1) of clause 1 of Article 14 of this Law and shall keep the information of the denouncer confidential; where it is detected that a terrorist activity has occurred, is occurring or there are grounds to believe that it is about to occur, they shall take the urgent counter-terrorism measures in accordance with the provisions of clause 2 of Article 16 of this Law.\n3. Upon receiving a notification or denunciation concerning terrorism, the counter-terrorism forces provided for in point (1) of clause 1 of Article 14 of this Law shall process it promptly and report to the competent agency and the competent counter-terrorism committee. Where it is detected that a terrorist activity has occurred, is occurring or there are grounds to believe that it is about to occur, they shall take the urgent counter-terrorism measures in accordance with the provisions of clause 2 of Article 16 of this Law.\n4. Where a terrorist activity occurs, the steering committee for counter-terrorism must report to the superior steering committee for counter-terrorism, and the counter-terrorism unit shall report directly to the superior counter-terrorism unit."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 29"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 30,
        "text": {
          "en": "Counter-terrorism measures\n1. The measures provided for in this Law and in the law on the protection of national security and the assurance of public order shall be taken to combat terrorism.\n2. Urgent counter-terrorism measures are measures taken immediately when a terrorist activity has occurred, is occurring or there are grounds to believe that it is about to occur ·211· The Law on Counter-Terrorism of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam in order to promptly stop the terrorist activity and to eliminate and limit the harm caused by terrorism. Urgent counter-terrorism measures comprise:\n(1) encircling and sealing off the area where the terrorist activity occurs;\n(2) rescuing hostages, providing emergency assistance to victims, isolating persons and moving means of transport and property out of the area of terrorist danger;\n(3) negotiating with terrorists;\n(4) encircling, pursuing, controlling and arresting terrorists and neutralising the weapons, tools and means used for terrorist activities;\n(5) attacking and eliminating terrorists and destroying the weapons, tools and means used for terrorist activities;\n(6) suspending the means of transport and the information and communication tools used for terrorist activities;\n(7) destroying and demolishing houses and structures obstructing counter-terrorism activities, removing obstacles obstructing counter-terrorism activities and setting up obstacles hindering terrorist activities;\n(8) protecting, moving, hiding and camouflaging the works and targets that are the objects of attack in terrorist activities;\n(9) mobilising forces and means to combat terrorism;\n(10) inspecting and freezing accounts and sources of funds related to terrorism, suspending transactions in funds and property related to terrorism and temporarily seizing funds and property related to terrorism;\n(11) opening, examining and seizing letters, telegrams, postal parcels, mail, packages and goods related to terrorism;\n(12) collecting materials and evidence related to terrorism.\n3. The Government shall make specific provisions on the competence, conditions, order and procedures for taking the urgent counter-terrorism measures provided for in clause 2 of this Article."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 30"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 31,
        "text": {
          "en": "Combating terrorism against the offices of diplomatic missions, foreign consular institutions and the representative offices of international organisations and the residences of their members\n1. Where there are grounds to believe that a terrorist activity has occurred, is occurring or is about to occur at the office of a diplomatic mission, a foreign consular institution or the representative office of an international organisation in Vietnam or at the residence of its members, the relevant agencies, organisations and individuals or persons with knowledge shall promptly notify the counter-terrorism forces provided for in point (1) of clause 1 of Article 14 of this Law or the nearest public security office, military unit or People's Committee. Upon receiving a notification or denunciation concerning terrorism, public security offices, military units and People's Committees shall receive and handle it in accordance with Article 29 of this Law.\n2. When carrying out counter-terrorism activities at the office of a diplomatic mission, a foreign consular institution or the representative office of an international organisation or at the residence of its members, Vietnamese agencies, organisations and individuals must comply with the provisions of this Law and of the international treaties to which the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is a party."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 31"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 32,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Combating terrorist activities against Vietnamese agencies, organisations and citizens abroad] Where there are grounds to believe that a terrorist activity has occurred, is occurring or is about to occur to a Vietnamese agency, organisation or citizen abroad, Belt and Road Legal Research, Volume 3 ·212· the head of the representative agency of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam abroad shall immediately take, within the scope of his or her competence, the necessary measures consistent with international law and the law of the host country and shall promptly report to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the National Steering Committee for Counter-Terrorism.\nChapter V COMBATING TERRORIST FINANCING"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 32"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 33,
        "text": {
          "en": "Detection of terrorist financing activities and receipt of notifications and denunciations of terrorist financing activities\n1. Where the State Bank, financial institutions, organisations and individuals engaged in non-financial sectors and other organisations and individuals detect signs and acts of terrorist financing, they shall promptly report them to the counter-terrorism forces provided for in point (1) of clause 1 of Article 14 of this Law.\n2. The counter-terrorism forces provided for in point (1) of clause 1 of Article 14 of this Law shall be responsible for receiving in full notifications and denunciations concerning terrorist financing and processing them promptly and reporting to the competent agency and the competent steering committee for counter-terrorism; upon detecting that a terrorist financing activity has occurred, is occurring or there are grounds to believe that it is about to occur, they shall immediately take the urgent counter-terrorism measures provided for in points (6), (9), (10), (11) and (12) of clause 2 of Article 30 of this Law."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 33"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 34,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Identification and updating of customer information and adoption of temporary measures] Financial institutions, organisations and individuals engaged in non-financial sectors shall be obliged to take measures to identify and update customer information; where there is suspicion that a customer or a transaction of a customer is related to terrorist financing or that the customer is included in a blacklist, they shall report to the counter-terrorism force of the Ministry of Public Security and the functional department of the State Bank of Vietnam and shall take temporary measures in accordance with the law on anti-money laundering."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 34"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 35,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Supervision of the cross-border movement of cash, precious metals, gemstones and negotiable instruments] Competent organisations and individuals supervising the movement of cash, precious metals, gemstones and negotiable instruments across the Vietnamese border in accordance with Article 24 of this Law and Article 24 of the Law on Anti-Money Laundering shall be responsible for promptly detecting, stopping and handling the use of such means for terrorist financing.\nChapter VI INTERNATIONAL COOPERATION IN COUNTER-TERRORISM"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 35"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 36,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Principles of international cooperation] The Socialist Republic of Vietnam shall carry out international cooperation in the field of counter-terrorism on the basis of compliance with Vietnamese law and the international treaties on counter-terrorism to which the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is a party, respect for the basic principles of international law, assurance of the independence, sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity of the Fatherland, and protection of national interests and the lawful rights and interests of organisations and individuals."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 36"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 37,
        "text": {
          "en": "Content of and responsibility for international cooperation\n1. The content of international cooperation comprises:\n(1) exchange of information on counter-terrorism;\n·213· The Law on Counter-Terrorism of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam\n(2) conduct of counter-terrorism training and exercises;\n(3) improvement of legal capacity in counter-terrorism and training and drilling in counter-terrorism knowledge and skills;\n(4) strengthening of the material conditions for counter-terrorism;\n(5) settlement of terrorism cases;\n(6) other content of international cooperation in accordance with the provisions of Vietnamese law and the international treaties to which the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is a party.\n2. The Ministry of Public Security shall preside over and coordinate with the relevant ministries in assisting the Government in negotiating, proposing the signing of or accession to international treaties relating to counter-terrorism and shall preside over and coordinate with the relevant ministries in carrying out counter-terrorism work."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 37"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 38,
        "text": {
          "en": "[International cooperation in the settlement of terrorism cases] International cooperation in the settlement of terrorism cases shall be carried out in accordance with the principles provided for in Article 4 and Article 36 of this Law and in the international treaties to which the Socialist Republic of Vietnam is a party. Where the Socialist Republic of Vietnam and the country concerned have not acceded to a multilateral treaty or signed a bilateral treaty, the competent agencies of Vietnam shall carry out cooperation with that State in the settlement of terrorism cases on the principles provided for in Article 4 and Article 36 of this Law and in accordance with the needs and capacity of the country.\nChapter VII RESPONSIBILITIES OF STATE AGENCIES IN COUNTER-TERRORISM WORK"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 38"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 39,
        "text": {
          "en": "State management agencies for counter-terrorism work\n1. The Government shall exercise unified State management of counter-terrorism work.\n2. The Ministry of Public Security shall be responsible to the Government and shall preside over and coordinate with the Ministry of National Defence and the relevant ministries in exercising State management of counter-terrorism work.\n3. People's Committees at all levels shall, within the scope of their functions and powers, be responsible for exercising State management of counter-terrorism work in their localities."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 39"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 40,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of the Ministry of Public Security\n1. The responsibilities of the Ministry of Public Security in State management of counter-terrorism are as follows:\n(1) to propose to the Government the formulation and improvement of the law on counter-terrorism;\n(2) to preside over and coordinate in formulating and submitting for promulgation, or in promulgating within its competence, legal normative documents, strategies, projects, plans, schemes and measures on counter-terrorism;\n(3) to preside over and coordinate with the relevant ministries and to direct provincial People's Committees in organising the implementation of legal normative documents, strategies, projects, plans, schemes and measures on counter-terrorism;\n(4) to preside over and coordinate with the Ministry of National Defence and the relevant agencies and organisations in issuing and organising the implementation of regulations on the training and fostering of counter-terrorism officials;\n(5) to preside over and coordinate with the relevant agencies and organisations in implementing the regime of reporting on and reviewing counter-terrorism work and in proposing and recommending solutions relating to counter- Belt and Road Legal Research, Volume 3 ·214· terrorism;\n(6) to supervise, inspect and settle complaints and denunciations in counter-terrorism work;\n(7) to carry out international cooperation in counter-terrorism in accordance with the provisions of clause 2 of Article 37 of this Law.\n2. The responsibilities of the Ministry of Public Security in organising and carrying out counter-terrorism work are as follows:\n(1) to equip and ensure equipment for the counter-terrorism force of the people's public security;\n(2) to preside over and coordinate with the relevant ministries, agencies and organisations in directing and organising the implementation of counter-terrorism work throughout the country in accordance with the provisions of Chapters III, IV and V of this Law, and to coordinate with the Ministry of National Defence in directing and organising the implementation of counter-terrorism work within its objects of management and its areas;\n(3) to direct the subordinate agencies and units in performing the tasks and exercising the powers provided for in Chapters III, IV and V of this Law and in detecting, investigating and handling in accordance with law organisations and individuals engaged in terrorism or terrorist financing;\n(4) to perform other tasks provided for in this Law and other relevant laws."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 40"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 41,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of the Ministry of National Defence\n1. To coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security in performing the tasks provided for in points (3) and (4) of clause 1 and point (2) of clause 2 of Article 40 of this Law.\n2. To preside over and coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security and the relevant agencies and organisations in carrying out counter-terrorism work at the targets and in the areas under the management of the Ministry of National Defence.\n3. To equip and ensure equipment for and direct the activities of the counter-terrorism force of the Ministry of National Defence.\n4. To direct the subordinate agencies and units in coordinating with the agencies and units of the people's public security in formulating, drilling, exercising and organising the implementation of plans for counter-terrorism.\n5. To direct the border guard force in coordinating with the agencies and units of the people's public security, the customs service and other agencies and units in implementing counter-terrorism measures through the supervision of persons leaving, entering or transiting at border gates.\n6. To coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs in carrying out international cooperation in counter-terrorism within its competence."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 41"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 42,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs\n1. To organise the implementation of counter-terrorism activities within the scope of its functions and powers in accordance with this Law and other relevant laws.\n2. To direct its subordinate agencies and units to prepare for participation in counter-terrorism work in accordance with the mobilisation decisions of persons with competence.\n3. To direct the heads of the missions of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam abroad to coordinate with the relevant authorities of the host country in counter-terrorism work.\n4. To coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security in formulating and organising the drilling and exercising of plans for counter-terrorism.\n5. Where a terrorist activity occurs, to coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security, the Ministry of National Defence and the localities where the offices of diplomatic missions, foreign consulates and representative offices of international organisations in Vietnam are located in formulating protection plans and response plans.\n6. To coordinate with the functional agencies in protecting the safety of foreign delegations visiting and performing official duties in Vietnam. Where a terrorist activity ·215· The Law on Counter-Terrorism of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam occurs, to coordinate with the relevant agencies and localities in managing and directing the press activities of foreign journalists.\n7. To coordinate with the diplomatic missions and consular missions in Vietnam of countries with a high incidence of terrorism in exchanging intelligence, proposing preventive and stopping measures and formulating, drilling and exercising various counter-terrorism scenarios.\n8. To coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security and other relevant ministries in carrying out international cooperation in counter-terrorism and to participate in the negotiation, signing, accession to and implementation of international treaties and international agreements on counter-terrorism."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 42"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 43,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of the Ministry of Transport\n1. To organise the implementation of counter-terrorism activities within the scope of its functions and powers in accordance with this Law and other relevant laws.\n2. To direct its subordinate agencies and units to prepare for participation in counter-terrorism work in accordance with the mobilisation decisions of persons with competence.\n3. To coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security, the Ministry of National Defence, the relevant ministries and local People's Committees in formulating, drilling, exercising and organising the implementation of plans for the prevention of and combat against the hijacking of aircraft, the hijacking of vessels and the taking of hostages and explosions on aircraft, vessels, trains and other means of transport, and in ensuring the security of airports, ports, railway stations and bus stations.\n4. To coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security, the Ministry of National Defence and local People's Committees in maintaining public order and security at important airports, railway stations, wharves, bus stations, seaports, bridges and road tunnels and in supervising drivers, passengers and means of transport so as to detect, stop and handle terrorist activities."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 43"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 44,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of the Ministry of Finance\n1. To organise the implementation of counter-terrorism activities within the scope of its functions and powers in accordance with this Law and other relevant laws.\n2. To direct its subordinate agencies and units to prepare for participation in counter-terrorism work in accordance with the mobilisation decisions of persons with competence.\n3. To direct the customs service in coordinating with the agencies of the people's public security, the border guard force and other relevant agencies in supervising goods and means of transport entering, leaving or transiting the country and in implementing counter-terrorism measures."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 44"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 45,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of the State Bank of Vietnam\n1. To organise the implementation of counter-terrorism activities within the scope of its functions and powers in accordance with this Law and other relevant laws.\n2. To direct its subordinate agencies and units to prepare for participation in counter-terrorism work in accordance with the mobilisation decisions of persons with responsibility.\n3. To receive information and reports from financial institutions and organisations and individuals engaged in non-financial sectors on suspicious transactions relating to terrorism and terrorist financing; where there are grounds to suspect that a transaction involves terrorism or terrorist financing, to promptly notify the counter-terrorism force of the Ministry of Public Security and to coordinate in verification.\n4. To coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security in carrying out international cooperation in counter-terrorism."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 45"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 46,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of the Ministry of Information and Communications\n1. To organise the implementation of counter-terrorism activities within the scope of its functions and powers in accordance with this Law and other relevant laws.\n2. To direct its subordinate agencies and units to prepare for participation in counter-terrorism work in accordance with the mobilisation decisions of persons with competence.\n3. To direct units and enterprises engaged in publication, the press, postal services, telecommunications and information technology in carrying out the following activities:\n(1) organising the assurance of information security for counter-terrorism activities.\n(2) coordinating with the public security and military agencies in formulating and carrying out counter-terrorism measures relating to publication, the press, postal services, telecommunications, information technology and communication network stations Belt and Road Legal Research, Volume 3 ·216· and in supervising activities relating to publication, the press, postal services, telecommunications and information technology so as to detect and handle the use of such activities for terrorist activities and terrorist financing activities.\n(3) controlling terrorist information published in the mass media, disseminating information on, educating and raising the awareness of officials and the people in counter-terrorism, and combating the information and communication activities of terrorist organisations and individuals."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 46"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 47,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of the relevant ministries in counter-terrorism work\n1. To organise the implementation of counter-terrorism activities within the scope of their functions and powers in accordance with this Law and other relevant laws.\n2. To coordinate with the Ministry of Public Security in exercising State management of counter-terrorism within the scope of their responsibilities.\n3. To direct their subordinate agencies and units to prepare for participation in counter-terrorism work in accordance with the mobilisation decisions of persons with competence."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 47"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 48,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Responsibilities of the People's Procuracies and the People's Courts] The People's Procuracies and the People's Courts shall, within the scope of their responsibilities, promptly handle offences of terrorism and terrorist financing and shall coordinate with the relevant agencies and organisations in carrying out counter-terrorism work in accordance with law."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 48"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 49,
        "text": {
          "en": "Responsibilities of People's Committees at all levels\n1. To exercise State management of counter-terrorism in their localities within the scope of their functions and powers and to organise the implementation of counter-terrorism activities in accordance with this Law and other relevant laws.\n2. To coordinate with the Vietnam Fatherland Front and socio-political organisations at the same level in launching mass movements to protect national security and to participate in counter-terrorism activities.\n3. To direct the local people's armed forces and functional agencies in formulating and carrying out local counter-terrorism work.\n4. To submit to the competent authorities the budget for counter-terrorism and to manage and use the budget for counter-terrorism in accordance with the law on the State budget.\nChapter VIII IMPLEMENTATION PROVISIONS"
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 49"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 50,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Effect] This Law shall take effect from 1 October 2013."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 50"
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 51,
        "text": {
          "en": "[Detailed provisions and guidance for implementation] The Government shall make detailed provisions on the articles of this Law and shall guide its implementation.\nThis Law was adopted on 12 June 2013 by the Fifth Session of the Thirteenth National Assembly of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 51"
        }
      }
    ]
  };

